  "body": "Trial enquiries and administrative student creation selected people by email; public trial requests could create credentials before later validation failed. Create unverified contacts and dependencies atomically with source-scoped retry keys. Public enquiries create no credentials or access grants. Student operations recheck school access and scope retries to the authenticated actor.\n\nConcurrent retries return the saved result, changed accepted input conflicts, and dependent failures roll back contact creation. Web forms retain keys after uncertain failures and edits. All three student dialogs block pending dismissal; abandoning a failed form requires explicit confirmation before clearing its key and starting a new operation.\n\nIncludes the reviewed commerce #436 and course #437 source, plus merged #434. Deploy these identity changes together. The trial migration adds private receipts and guarded references; empty rollback works and used receipts refuse destructive rollback. Native contract companion #103 is merged. Native publication remains blocked by the physical-iOS Google sign-in gate; no physical device is available.\n\nVerified: six dedicated PostgreSQL regressions; 2,586 backend examples with zero failures before the later course integration (five separately exercised PostgreSQL suites pending in the general run); nine trial-page tests plus three rendered student-dialog lifecycle regressions; web/mobile TypeScript, focused lint and strict catalog audit. Staging migration replay, backup restoration and private ACL checks passed. The latest combined source must pass hosted CI. Application staging verification and production deployment remain pending. See docs/identity/trial-prevention.md.\n\nFollow-up review fixes: unchanged shared student emails remain editable without weakening authorization. Ad inquiries now use a required source request key and atomic private contact/lead receipt; email/phone cannot adopt a person or grant student access. A committed notification reservation prevents retries from repeating replies; uncertain deliveries remain visible for operator review. The unused legacy account-provisioning helper is removed. There is no bundled ad submission form; the handwritten client now requires its caller to provide a stable key. External clients without a key receive 400 before writes.\n\nThe final manifest preserves all 110 approved main entries, including calendar runtime, then appends course, trial and ad inquiry migrations (113 total). All 113 migrations, repeated application, staging backup restoration and private ACL verification passed. New student-edit and ad inquiry PostgreSQL regressions are awaiting hosted CI on the latest combined head; no passing result is claimed yet. Intake staging HTTP tests passed and the newer independently deployed production e1a825bd includes intake. Final combined staging HTTP validation and deployment remain pending.\n",
